+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid complete visit submission, the system SHALL store it as an immutable visit revision carrying its visit ID, author ID, server receipt time, and base revision ID (or no base for a root submission).
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When an authenticated worker repeats an idempotency key that the system accepted from that worker with an identical canonical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored revision.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When an authenticated worker repeats an idempotency key that the system accepted from that worker with a different canonical payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original revision unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When two or more revisions are derived from the same starting revision, the system SHALL preserve every such revision regardless of the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When an authenticated caller retrieves a visit with unresolved review work, the system SHALL return the competing active frontier revisions (revisions with no accepted child that remain candidates for the current state) and indicate that no revision is current.
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL record the coordinator's identity, the selected revision ID, and the contributing revision IDs (the reviewed active frontier set) with the resolution.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit whose base revision is the visit's sole active frontier revision, the system SHALL accept the new revision as the current revision without review.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit whose base revision is not the visit's sole active frontier revision, the system SHALL accept the new revision as a competing active revision and mark the visit unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit without a base revision for a visit that already has revisions, the system SHALL accept the submission as a competing root revision (a revision with no base revision) and mark the visit unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit with a base revision that does not belong to that visit, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: While a visit has exactly one active revision, the system SHALL report the visit as current and identify that revision as its current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator resolves an unresolved visit, the system SHALL select one reviewed active frontier revision as current, mark the other reviewed active frontier revisions as not selected, and mark the visit current.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a coordinator submits a resolution whose reviewed active frontier revisions or frontier version (a counter that changes whenever the active frontier changes) no longer match the visit's active frontier, the system SHALL reject the resolution without changing the visit.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a coordinator submits a resolution for a visit that has no unresolved review work, the system SHALL reject the resolution without changing the visit.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When a coordinator submits a resolution whose selected revision is not in the reviewed active frontier, the system SHALL reject the resolution without changing the visit.
+- [ ] **REC-016**: The system SHALL retain every accepted revision, including superseded and not-selected revisions, for retrieval in the visit's revision history.
+- [ ] **REC-017**: When an authenticated caller retrieves a visit's revision history, the system SHALL return each revision's payload, author, receipt time, base revision ID, and status.
+- [ ] **REC-018**: When a coordinator requests the unresolved review queue, the system SHALL return the visits with unresolved review work, their competing active frontier revisions, and each visit's frontier version.
+- [ ] **REC-019**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit whose plot reference is not present in the catalog (archived plots remain present), the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a caller without the coordinator role attempts to resolve review work, the system SHALL reject the resolution without changing the visit.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit whose payload is invalid, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: The system SHALL determine the current revision from the revision graph and SHALL NOT use arrival order as evidence of scientific authority.
+- [ ] **REC-023**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit that does not exist with no base revision, the system SHALL create the visit and store the revision as its current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-024**: When an authenticated caller retrieves a current visit, the system SHALL return the current revision's payload, author, and receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-025**: When an authenticated caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return the visit's frontier version.
+- [ ] **REC-026**: The system SHALL NOT combine field values from different revisions when resolving review work.
+- [ ] **REC-027**: When an authenticated caller retrieves a visit's resolution history, the system SHALL return each resolution's coordinator, selected revision, contributing revisions, and resolution time.
+- [ ] **REC-028**: When a caller without the coordinator role requests the unresolved review queue, the system SHALL reject the request.
+- [ ] **REC-029**: When a coordinator requests the unresolved review queue, the system SHALL order the visits by the oldest active frontier receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-030**: When the system rejects a resolution as stale, the system SHALL return the visit's current active frontier revisions and frontier version.
